Adapted for Blah default reactions by blah-reaction-art contributors (2026).
Changes: normalized and centered on 512 x 512 canvases using the source's "rest"
marker (frame 0 when absent); rotated native-speed loops to that pose after a lead-in
hold; froze it for static icons, entrances and holds; center uses 55% scale;
added entrance scaling/fades, activation rotation and separate palette-derived
circle/diamond particle effects; rebased copied clocks for short frozen outputs
while retaining live source clocks, interpolation and stretch;
removed exporter metadata, redundant defaults and identity merge operators; retained
vector precompositions, source time remapping/stretch and alpha/inverted-alpha track mattes;
encoded as deterministic gzip TGS and lossless transparent WebP.
Noto's FAQ identifies the static "start" frame as keyframe "rest" (link above).
Source markers are consumed during conversion and omitted from outputs.
